\title{D-KR-07 · Labelled shapes \code{Θ_{T,X}}}
\taxon{Decision}
\meta{id}{D-KR-07}
\meta{area}{kernel}
\meta{origin}{design/01-kernel.md}
\meta{status}{superseded}
\meta{status-text}{frozen.}
\meta{supersedes}{none}
\meta{superseded-by}{dec-kr-0019}
\tag{decision}
\tag{area:kr}
\tag{status:superseded}

\subtree{
  \title{Decision}
  \p{For \code{X : Type u}, \code{Θ_{T,X} := ∫_{Θ_T} X^{ob(−)}}, the category of elements of the presheaf \code{θ ↦ (ob θ → X)} where \code{ob : Θ_T → Set} gives the object positions of a shape. Objects are labelled shapes, morphisms are shape maps preserving labels. A function \code{X → Y} induces \code{Θ_{T,X} → Θ_{T,Y}}.}
}
\subtree{
  \title{Rationale}
  \p{Gepner–Haugseng's \code{Δ_X} generalized. Labels discretize objects: Segal conditions over object positions become products.}
}
\subtree{
  \title{Acceptance}
  \p{\ref{at-kr-0009}: \code{Δ_X} agrees with the labelled simplex construction; the Segal condition on \code{Δ_X} characterizes categories with object set \code{X} (unbiased form).}
}
\subtree{
  \title{Status}
  \p{frozen.}
}
